<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shakhbut bin Sultan Al Nahyan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1905">1905</a>–<a href="/years/1989">1989</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shakhbut bin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-nahyan">Al Nahyan</a> was ruler of Abu Dhabi from 1928 to 1966. His long reign saw the collapse of the pearl trade and the discovery of oil, which was first exported in 1962, but his reluctance to spend the new revenues frustrated his family and the British. In 1966 he was replaced by his brother Zayed in a bloodless change of power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shakhbut-bin-sultan-al-nahyan.jpg" alt="Shakhbut bin Sultan Al Nahyan" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Prince UAE at Arabic Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B4%D9%8A%D8%AE_%D8%B3%D9%84%D8%B7%D8%A7%D9%86_%D8%A8%D9%86_%D8%B2%D8%A7%D9%8A%D8%AF_19-1-1961.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
